id="guide-land">Find land</button><button id="repeat-guide">First steps</button></div><p><span id="mode-explanation">This sandbox starts with plants and rabbits. It does not yet evolve simple life into new plant or animal groups. Suggestions reflect the current planet, not required levels or guaranteed survival.</span></p><details id="manual"><summary>Controls and field notes</summary><div id="origin-fields" hidden><p>Turquoise mats mark real microbial biomass. Tap <b>Habitat</b> to find shallow water; <b>Seed</b> introduces an existing colony. <b>Nutr. +</b> is a deliberate external nutrient input, not food created by the ecosystem.</p><p>Simple seeds need 0.2–50 m water above 0°C, usable light and resources. Evolved producers with actual paid support and inherited structure can exploit thinner liquid films; the 15–20 cm transition also permits partial aquatic growth. No photosynthesis occurs when dry or frozen. Grazing and movement still require aquatic conditions. Inspect shows carbon biomass, nutrients and the dominant living lineage. Descendants can develop aquatic producer forms: cushion, rosette, ribbon, branching and canopy. Shapes follow inherited traits and actual support tissue; these are not terrestrial plant species or animals.</p><p><b>Habitat care:</b> Use <b>Find habitat → Shape nursery → Seed colony → Watch life</b> for a shallow starting patch. Nursery shapes a 5 m center beside a 15 m reservoir and dry rim; it supplies water once, not new organisms. Press Play if paused. The older level 15 m basin is still available in Life snapshot. Inspect shallow patches as water changes. For routine replenishment, a <b>Water +</b> tap adds 1 m to the selected patch. For precision, open <b>Life snapshot</b> and choose <b>Set 0.5 m</b>. Both supply water once: there is no automatic refill or guaranteed evolution.</p></div><div id="sandbox-fields"><p><b>Read the map:</b> tan is bare land, blue is water, green is vegetation, and orange dots mark living rabbits. Close-up sprouts show real vegetated patches, not individual plant counts; they grow with coverage and shrink when grazed. Rabbit models stand on the surface when you zoom close.</p><p><b>1. Find your land.</b> Tap <b>Land</b> below the game to jump to dry ground. Use <b>＋</b> to get close and <b>Globe</b> to return to a whole-planet view.</p><p><b>2. Shape a habitat.</b> Use Land +/− and Water +/−. Dry land supports rabbits; deep water does not. Pause while sculpting. Water and land brushes respond to how long you hold, not simulation speed. Inspect shows water depth.</p><p><b>3. Plant the land.</b> Choose Plants and paint patches of vegetation. Rabbits eat it, so establish food before adding animals.</p><p><b>4. Add rabbits.</b> Choose Rabbits, then tap suitable land. Watch the population and inspect the surface temperature. This prototype currently has vegetation and rabbits, not a full multi-species ecosystem.</p></div><p><b>Always daylight</b> keeps the side you are viewing lit while the climate simulation continues. You can change the view in the planet menu.</p><p>Tap menu buttons and the tool buttons inside the game. Choose a tool, then touch the planet to use it.</p><p><b>Pinch with two fingers</b> to zoom smoothly. In <b>Navigate</b> mode, drag one finger to explore and tap to use a menu or selected tool. Switch to <b>Paint</b> to brush plants or terrain by dragging. Pinching never finishes as a tool tap. Zoom +/− also works.</p><p>Landscape gives you more room. Full screen hides the browser bars. The game automatically resizes when you rotate.</p><p><b>More → Save / Load:</b> Save keeps one planet in this browser on this device, including its ecosystem. It is not a cloud backup. Wait for the Saved message before closing. Clearing site data or using a private browsing session can remove it. Load replaces your unsaved world.</p><p><b>Mobile detail:</b> New browser planets use a lighter grid for smoother play and smaller saves. Existing saved worlds keep their original grid detail when loaded.</p><p>Pause, settings and tool details are now in the game, above the planet. Open <b>More → Speed / fast-forward</b> to choose a target of 1, 6 or 24 simulated hours per real second. The top pace button also cycles these targets. Achieved speed is measured separately and may be lower on your device. New worlds start with the 6-hour target; saved worlds keep their requested pace. Pause to sculpt or inspect. Faster time also dries water faster, so watch your habitat.</p></details><a href="qa.html">Executed gameplay tests</a> · <a href="source.html">GPL source</a> · <a href="LICENSE">License</a></section><aside id="gameplay-measure-status" hidden aria-live="polite"><span id="gameplay-measure-message"></span><button id="cancel-gameplay-measure">Cancel</button></aside></main><script src="gameplay-measure.js"></script><script src="touch-controls.js"></script><script src="stella-storage.js"></script><script src="life-trend.js"></script><script>
